Departure_from_Maxwell's_equations:
  - a_toroid_always_has_a_magnetic_field_and_does_not_need_relative_motion
  - a_displacement_current_is_superfluous
  - electromagnetic_induction_(which_is_how_the_hyperfine_shift_works)_consists_of_a_redistribution_of_changing_Sp-2_magnetic_momentum_into_Sp-3_electric_momentum_to_preserve_action_h,_there_is_no_electric_field_created_in_the_surrounding_space
  - the_photon_(HS)_is_the_basic_element_and_its_Sp-2_and_Sp-3_rotations_produce_the_magnetic_and electric_momentum_fields,_a_photon_is_not_the_result_of_time-varying_fields
  - Coulomb's_law_is_the_displacement_of_Sp-3_momentum_into_translational_momentum_by_the_intruding_rotating_Sp-3_field_and_so_is_a_local_interaction
  - charge_is_not_an_intrinsic_scalar_property_but_is_defined_by_four_Sp-2/Sp-3_chiralities
  - even_though_the_PTV_model_has_Sp-2_rotation_as_the_generator_of_magnetic_momentum_field,_Ampere's_law_results_from_aligned_electron_Sp-3_toroids_creating_Sp-3_fields_which_rotate_around_a_current_carrying_conductor
  - in_Ampere's_law,_the_magnetic_field_surrounding_a_current-carrying_conductor_consists_of_electron_Sp-3_field_rotation

Lorentz_force_mechanism:
  - the_magnetic_field_(from_Ampere's_law_analysis)_is_a_p3f_momentum_field_derived_from_electron_Sp-3_rotation
  - the_electron_toroid_consists_of_an_Sp-2_circuit_that_adopts_various_orientations_as_it_passes_around_the_toroid_at_speed_alpha*c
  - the_toroid_approaches_the_p3f_field_across_its_path_at_speed_v
  - the_field_has_a_gradient,_being_stronger_nearer_the_source_than_further_away
  - due_to_the_toroid's_speed_through_the_field,_relative_to_the_toroid_there_is_a_component_of_the_p3f_momentum_directed_towards_it
  - this_component_also_has_a_gradient
  - when_the_Sp-2_circuit_is_nearest_the_source,_one_side_of_the_Sp-2_circuit_receives_a_greater_momentum_component_than_the_other_resulting_in_a_net_increase_or_decrease_in_action_integrated_around_the_circuit
  - this_action_is_either_given_to_or_taken_away_from_its_Sp-3_speed_v3,_so_v3_increases_for_an_action_overload_and_decreases_for_an_underload
  - this_Sp-2_circuit_consequently_deflects_perpendicular_to_both_field_and_toroidal_velocity_v_due_to_the_Sp-3_speed_change
  - when_the_Sp-2_circuit_is_furthest_away_from_the_source,_both_its_rotation_sense_and_Sp-3_speed_are_inverted
  - so_whereas_nearest_the_source_there_might_have_been_an_action_overlaod_it_is_now_an_underload_so_the_Sp-3_speed_decreases_to_compensate
  - the_combination_of_reversed_Sp-3_speed-change_and_reversed_Sp-3_direction_means_the_Sp-2_circuit_deflects_the_same_way_in_both_positions
  - this_replaces_a_law_of_association_with_a_real_mechanism_that_adopts_the_fundamental_postulate_(2)

